    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The infamous prison The Clink, whose name gave rise to the word for jail, was located in Southwark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwark"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Southwark Cathedral, originally the priory of St Mary Overie, is London’s oldest church south of the Thames.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwark"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1836 Southwark saw the launch of London’s first railway, the London and Greenwich Railway, ending at Spa Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwark"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Southwark is the place from which the Mayflower originally set sail for the New World, though it officially departed from Plymouth.",
